# CRC Cards (Studio Step 70–92)


---

## CRC-01: Student

| Responsibilities | Collaborators |
|---|---|
| Join a Virtual Queue for a Registration Service | Virtual Queue, Registration Service |
| Hold at most one active Queue Entry per Registration Service (BR-04 / one-active-entry rule) | Queue Entry |
| Book an Appointment against an available Appointment Slot (BR-01) | Appointment, Appointment Slot |
| Cancel an Appointment, subject to Cancellation Policy (BR-05, BR-08) | Appointment, Cancellation Rule |
| Receive notification of a Queue Status or Appointment change | Queue Entry, Appointment |

---

## CRC-02: Virtual Queue

| Responsibilities | Collaborators |
|---|---|
| Maintain an ordered collection of Queue Entries for one Registration Service | Queue Entry, Registration Service |
| Track open/closed state and capacity | Registration Service Administrator |
| Assign Queue Position to each new Queue Entry in join order (BR-06) | Queue Entry |
| Determine the next eligible Queue Entry to call (Service/call-order Rule) | Queue Entry, Service Rule |
| Enforce Queue Availability before accepting a new entry (BR-03) | Registration Service |

---

## CRC-03: Queue Entry

| Responsibilities | Collaborators |
|---|---|
| Record the Student, Virtual Queue, Queue Number, and Queue Position it belongs to | Student, Virtual Queue |
| Track its own Queue Status (waiting, called, completed) | Virtual Queue |
| Transition status when called or completed, and prevent re-entry into an active queue once completed | Registration Staff |
| Enforce uniqueness of active entry per Student/Service (BR-04) | Student, Registration Service |

---

## CRC-04: Appointment

| Responsibilities | Collaborators |
|---|---|
| Link a Student to a specific Appointment Slot | Student, Appointment Slot |
| Validate availability before booking (BR-01) | Appointment Slot |
| Prevent a second active Appointment for the same Student/Service (BR-04) | Student, Registration Service |
| Apply Cancellation Policy on cancellation requests (BR-05, BR-08) | Cancellation Rule |
| Mark itself completed and become immutable thereafter (BR-08) | Registration Staff |

---

## CRC-05: Appointment Slot

| Responsibilities | Collaborators |
|---|---|
| Represent a single bookable time slot for a Registration Service | Registration Service |
| Report its own availability | Appointment |
| Prevent being double-booked (BR-02) | Appointment, Registration Staff |
| Belong to exactly one Service Provider/Registration Staff assignment (BR-07) | Registration Staff |

---

## CRC-06: Registration Staff (Service Provider)

| Responsibilities | Collaborators |
|---|---|
| Call the next eligible Queue Entry (FR-10) | Virtual Queue, Queue Entry |
| Manage Appointments only for their assigned Registration Service (BR-07) | Appointment, Registration Service |
| Mark a Queue Entry or Appointment as completed | Queue Entry, Appointment |
| Cannot modify or reopen a completed Appointment (BR-08) | Appointment |
